#Estimates how much energy and CO₂ each LLM model consumed on the DIANE platform between October and December 2025. 
It pulls usage data (tokens, requests) and GPU power measurements from our shared S3 bucket, 
looks up model sizes on HuggingFace, and splits total cluster energy across models proportionally to their computational load. 
Results include energy per model (kWh), carbon footprint (kg CO₂), and efficiency metrics (Wh per request, kWh per million tokens). 
Run it directly on Onyxia — credentials and S3 endpoint are picked up automatically from the environment.#
"""
DIANE Energy Analysis – Per-Model Energy & CO₂ Estimation
==========================================================
This script estimates how much energy and CO₂ each LLM model consumed
on the DIANE platform. It pulls usage data (tokens, requests) and GPU
power measurements from our shared S3 bucket, looks up model sizes on
HuggingFace, and splits total cluster energy across models proportionally
to their computational load.

Results include:
  - Energy per model (kWh), carbon footprint (kg CO₂)
  - Efficiency metrics: Wh per request, kWh per million tokens
  - Two uptime scenarios (optimistic vs pessimistic) to reflect
    uncertainty about when the cluster is actually running

Run directly on Onyxia — S3 credentials are picked up automatically
from the environment (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN, S3_ENDPOINT).

Usage:
  python diane_energy_analysis.py
  python diane_energy_analysis.py --no-hf       # skip HuggingFace lookup
  python diane_energy_analysis.py --no-export   # do not write results to S3
"""

